## 16) Release Readiness Criteria

A release is ready only if:

* Critical workflows tested in staging
* Migration/rollback validated
* Monitoring dashboards and alerts updated
* Runbook updated with known risks
* KPI measurement window and owner assigned
* Feature flags configured for gradual rollouts
* CI/CD pipeline running for zero-downtime deploys
* Database backups automated with tested restore process
* CDN enabled
* Auto-scaling configured for traffic spikes
* Payment processor integration via Stripe
* Subscription lifecycle implemented: trials, upgrades, downgrades, cancellations
* Webhooks configured for payment activities
* Invoicing and receipts automated
* Refund policy defined (14-day no questions)
* Pricing page live with 3 subscription tiers displayed (starter, pro, enterprise)
* Accessibility Basics Implemented: keyboard navigation, screen reader support, proper contrast ratios
* Performance optimized: page load under 3 seconds, API responses under 200ms
* Error handling and 404/500 pages in place
* Onboarding flow completes in under 2 minutes with a guided tour
* Core workflow tested end to end on desktop and mobile

## 17) Mandatory Startup Sequence for Reconstruction

1. Collect Base44/OpenAPI/workflow inputs and screenshots
2. Publish architecture plan and multi-tenant boundaries
3. Publish repo scaffold and schema plan
4. Publish feature-by-feature rebuild plan
5. # Implement only after architecture approval
